                        "form": "more dreamish"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "26a068ed-baa9-4768-816a-2fc39c2411fa",
                        "entry_id": "6ce93dc3-7ec5-3557-b215-b7951b690afe",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most dreamish"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69a8b47c-d654-3775-905c-1ed2c501f906",
                        "entry_id": "6ce93dc3-7ec5-3557-b215-b7951b690afe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a dream or the state of dreaming."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b83b69e-d63f-4baf-ae63-a002a919a7ff",
                                "sense_id": "69a8b47c-d654-3775-905c-1ed2c501f906",
                                "text": "Sometimes a faintish, dizzy feeling flits through my brain, the ground and the mountains begin to quiver. The shout of a Bedouin rouses me from a dreamish stupor, to a keener desire for water. O for a cup of the cold water at my father's door!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9e2dc2e-1b4c-4338-a480-a0b2d0d44301",
                                "sense_id": "69a8b47c-d654-3775-905c-1ed2c501f906",
                                "text": "Instead of getting drowsier she was getting more awake—with an odd night-time, dreamish kind of wakefulness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b965c3e4-1533-4c63-aa9e-1c8308624772",
                                "sense_id": "69a8b47c-d654-3775-905c-1ed2c501f906",
                                "text": "The dreamish, arational quality of Baraka's poems is of a piece with his contempt for the confusion of rationality with rationalization (“Bankrupt utopia sez tell me / no utopias”)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3237d19-c785-43a6-a381-bd62440dabba",
                                "sense_id": "69a8b47c-d654-3775-905c-1ed2c501f906",
                                "text": "It was fatigued thinking, dreamish thinking. She didn't even believe in spirits. But she recalled him standing firm in the waterfall current; she saw him pop up, desert dry, onto the top of Vance's trailer while it bobbed in the river; she saw her bookcase standing upright to cover the hole in her bedroom wall."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
